From 81863fefbbaf0ee0757387237e620b77e73528a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Local compatibility investigation <local@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:39:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: service small image shared pages through aliases

Keep small writable shared x64 PE sections coherent on a 16 KB host without
sharing or overwriting their neighbouring private sections. Cover the observed
DOOM 2016 and Vulkan executable layouts with a guarded, non-executable-page
fallback. Keep true shared aliases, enforce logical guest permissions, use
canonical atomic operations, and drain fault readers before retiring aliases.
Decline native-code overlap, loader directories, shared-target relocations and
unsupported instruction forms instead of substituting private data.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: tools/tests/test_image_shared.py; real shared-alias host checks and isolated iOS ARM64 component compile passed; full Wine build and phone gate pending
Offered-upstream: no; local candidate pending full native build and device validation
